 "updated": "2026-07-17 12:05:27",
 "new_data_finding": "Attempted 2 NEW belief-gated generated sets (new_hpkr_terse terse knowledge-denial; new_agentic_matched record-vs-report) on the board suspect Qwen3.5-27B with a real 5-vote belief gate. RESULT: could not be made leak-free. Under a strong directive the model denies/conceals ~100% but the DIRECTIVE leaks (blindnull ~1.0); under a moderate or discretionary directive the base model answers/discloses ~100% (no lie class, 0/354 denials, 0/240 concealments across 3 prompt strengths). This empirically reproduces the AISI/LB thesis that behaviour-verified deception on a base model is either instruction-leaky or non-existent -> you need a fine-tuned ORGANISM. The gauntlet's leak-free terse-denial coverage therefore comes from the real ORGANISM + real-bench sets (lb_hp_kr 0.43, lb_gender 0.46, wf_denial 0.40, dyl_ab_denial 0.54). build_new.py (belief gate + generation + dual-judge behaviour labelling) is validated and reusable the moment an organism is served.",
 "name": "deception-detection held-out gauntlet",
 "purpose": "Broad held-out deception-test substrate: diverse distributions our detectors were never tuned on, to measure real generalization. Import gauntlet.py; iterate list_dists(); load_dist(name) -> (rows, srows, y). Score any reader vs every distribution.",
 "discipline": "behaviour-verified / belief-relative labels (Liar's Bench section 3); per-dist nulls (lennull + reply-withheld blindnull) measured BEFORE scoring; leaky-context dists FLAGGED not silently dropped; a failure RAISES, never returns a null.",
 "suspect_note": "every row carries the NDIF-served suspect for its generator family (auto-mapped in gauntlet.suspect_for); rows whose true generator is off-substrate get Qwen3.5-27B as a cross-model 3rd-person audit (documented, same as research_genaudit_external).",
